A||N||6||85Josh||Windows 98SE Install CD?||||1||
Z||000000||85Josh||09-10-2001||09:18 PM||||OK, here's my problem. I bought an Emachines PC (I know,I know!). Now I'm trying to upgrade it, to include a new mobo that supports more memory. Problem is, the emachines restore cd won't let me reinstall windows, which has gotten corrupted, because it can tell that it's not an emachines mobo. So, can anyone tell me where to get a Windows 98se Install CD to use with my license number? I don't want to pay three hundred bucks! TIA!<P>Josh<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||09-10-2001||11:23 PM||||Have you wiped out the old HDD yet?  It should have a folder on it called CABS, usually c:\Windows\options\cabs on most PC's.  The CABS folder is your Windows install CD.  Just copy those files onto your HDD, boot from a floppy, and run setup.exe.  Same a running it from the CD.||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||09-11-2001||05:22 AM||||Thanks, formula, but somehow, the Cabs Setup is customized to an Emachine mobo, too. I tried that, but it is still no-go.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||09-11-2001||06:50 AM||||fdisk||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||09-11-2001||09:12 AM||||The CABS folder should work.  Try copying everything from CABS off the PC, then fdisk and reformat (also, do an fdisk /mbr to format your master boot record).  Then copy the CABS back over and try it then.  I don't have experience with Emachines, but with Compaq and IBM, the restore CD checks for machine type, but the CABS folder does not.||||reg||6
Z||000005||85Josh||09-11-2001||11:56 AM||||Thanks, I'll give it a shot. Right now, I'm glued to the TV, since I'm in the National Guard.||||reg||1
